#: itemlist_brimhaven2.json:book_world_history
#: itemlist_brimhaven2.json:book_world_history_complete
msgid "World History"
msgstr "Istòria de su mundu"

#: itemlist_brimhaven2.json:book_world_history:description
msgid ""
"* by Wormath Splathershed * \n"
"\n"
"Foundation of the Forgotten Kingdom (year 2300)\n"
"The first humans, led by Arntuk the Mighty, came from the south in ancient times and established the Forgotten Kingdom. These people, called the Lethgar, built settlements in places where now great towns and cities are located. Nor City and Sullengard were the first to be founded.\n"
"Then some time later, a few explorers climbed Mount Galmore, the highest mountain in Dhayavar. Due to the elevation and marvelous view, their priests and mages built a sanctuary near the summit where they studied the arts of magic and worshipped their gods. \n"
"\n"
"Rise of Kazaul (year 2177)\n"
"The insane and powerful wizard called Valugha was obsessed with the notion of creating a portal to another plane. Even though his fellow mages disapproved, he was able to create a portal by consuming the powerful life essence of his brothers and the stored energy in the sanctuary. The sanctuary erupted in an explosion and a large ravine split Mt. Galmore apart. At its bottom, the portal opened, which was soon merely called the 'Rift', and the devastated area around it 'Undertell'. The mountain also spilled out lava like blood coming from a wound and is now clouded in smoke all the time.\n"
"All kinds of demons and undead emerged into the world through the portal, led by their masters, the 'Kazaul'. The Kazaul themselves were guided by the Eternal Masters who were incredibly skilled in magic and warcraft. Soon the monsters and their masters spread over whole of Dhayavar. However, the portal became unstable after a while and finally collapsed after several decades, but the harm was already done, as thousands of beasts had crept through it into the realm. \n"
"A short and brutal war was fought. With the loss of nearly all mages, the Lethgar were powerless against the monster invasion and were soon overthrown and enslaved by the Kazaul. The Kazaul imposed a reign of terror on the Forgotten Kingdom. It seemed no one was able to defeat or oppose the Kazaul due to their inhuman strength. \n"
"Then the Lethgar had to build underground lairs for their oppressors. A large city was built around the deactivated portal and in the natural caves under Mt. Galmore. Also, Carn Tower and the Sanctuary on Blackwater Mountain were built, among countless other underground Kazaul settlements.\n"
"Even though most Lethgar despised their masters, some showed interest in the rituals and dark sorcery of the Kazaul. As a result, the Kha'zaan (Kazaul cultists), a group of human Kazaul followers, gathered around their masters and learned from them. They were often used to enforce the brutal rule of the Kazaul. Many of the current monsters are living forms that evolved from experiments made during this era, such as Izthiels, Gornauds, Wyrms, etc.\n"
"By that time, the Hira'zinn, the omen of war, started plaguing the smallfolk. \n"
"\n"
"The War of Dawn and the Rise of Elythara and the Elytharan Union (year 1537)\n"
"One day, the Elytharan cultists arrived on the shore of the northern sea (Sea of Tears). They worshipped the blinding and cleansing light of Elythara. \n"
"The Elytharan mages and warriors were able to defeat the Kazaul and Kha'zaan with the help of the blinding light of Elythara which was forged\n"
"\n"
"[... here some pages were torn out ...]\n"
"\n"
"began erecting the city of Feygard on the shore of the Sea of Tears, which soon became a center of trade for the realm due to its access to the sea. \n"
"The town of Loneford was founded and it soon became famous for its fertile fields and healthy vegetable which fed the northern parts of the Forgotten Kingdom. \n"
"Blackwater Mountain was explored, and on its summit a large sanctuary for the Elytharan priests was erected to study dawn and dusk, the sun and stars, and to watch over the Forgotten Kingdom. Other sanctuaries were located in Feygard and Nor City, and shrines were found in each minor settlement. The mining colony of Prim was also founded after pioneers found rich sources of iron and coal under the mountain.\n"
"The city of Fallhaven became a prosperous center of trade due to its excellent location as a junction between the sanctuary of Blackwater Mountain, Stoutford, Nor City and Feygard. Big storehouses were built to safely store shipments. However, bands of thieves were soon attracted by the growing wealth, and united under one big organization, the Thieves' Guild, whose guild halls were secretly placed in Fallhaven, Feygard, and Nor City, those being the richest cities at that time. \n"
"Many other towns, including Brimhaven and Brightport were also founded around this time, and the Charwood mines were opened.\n"
"Trade agreements were signed between the cities in order to make trade prosper further. \n"
"\n"
"Establishment of the Aewatha Kingdom (year 432)\n"
"The head of the most important Nor City family, Garthan I of house Houdart, declared himself King, marking the end of the Elytharan era and the beginning of the Shadow-supported kingdom. At this point, political power and religious power became closely united. As the kingdom prospered, so did the Shadow, and Elythara\n"
"\n"
"[... again some pages were torn out ...]\n"
"\n"
"as slaves for the digging. At that time the Flagstone Prison was also built, where runaway workers from Mt. Galmore were imprisoned and were left to rot. However the mines were closed after some years due to frequent monster attacks and other unspeakable horrors who dwelt in the dark.\n"
"Remgard was founded by Korhald of Remgard and built on a large island in Lake Laeroth. It became famous for its excellent smithing services. \n"
"The village of Crossglen was founded, and farmers settled there.\n"
"King Luthor ascended to the throne as the direct heir of King Oromir III and moved the capital from Nor City to Fallhaven, while the center of worship remained in Nor City. As King Luthor got older he felt the need for an advisor, and so Lord Geomyr of Feygard was named Hand of the King. He fulfilled his duty with great obsession and effort. \n"
"\n"
"The Noble Wars (year 25 to 14)\n"
"When King Luthor died, he left the Kingdom with no heir to the throne. He was buried in the catacombs under Fallhaven church. What followed, the Noble Wars, was one of the darkest periods this country has witnessed. \n"
"Four coalitions were formed which were each ruled by one powerful Lord. \n"
"The Western one consisted of Stoutford and the settlements on Blackwater Mountain, and was ruled by Lord Erwyn. \n"
"The Northern one consisted of Feygard, Thalgard, Luthaven and Remgard, and was ruled by Lord Geomyr. \n"
"The Eastern one consisted of Nor City, Sullengard, Brightport and Brimhaven, and was ruled by Lord Emeric. \n"
"The center capital area at first remained neutral and consisted of Fallhaven, Vilegard and Loneford (formerly administrated by King Luthor). \n"
"The Noble Wars started with the Landlords arguing about who was to be the new, legitimate, King. \n"
"The first stone was thrown by Stoutford. Lord Erwyn tried to use the time to attack the center area when the other Lords were busy debating. He wanted to occupy those to control the trade routes to Nor City, to gain the largest influence and to fracture other coalitions. Fallhaven was partially destroyed.\n"
"Erwyn's success was a short one, as he was attacked by the Eastern coalition. For several years, numerous battles and countless skirmishes were fought over control of the center area. When both Lords were weakened, Lord Geomyr attacked and forced both to surrender. The peace treaty of Fallhaven was signed and Lord Geomyr was proclaimed King.\n"
"The Hira'zinn haunted the lands once again during the war. \n"
"\n"
"The Rule of King Geomyr (year 14)\n"
"King Geomyr urged people to restore the destroyed cities and remove the traces of the long war. He reinstated a tax system, and garrisons of the Royal Guard of Feygard, in most of the villages. Geomyr promoted nepotism and corruption to further increase his power.\n"
"The cult of the Shadow became ever more important for the smallfolk. The commoners felt the need for salvation after the harsh period of the Noble Wars and accepted the Shadow as their guide into better times.\n"
"Lord Geomyr became fearful of the power of the religion, and tensions between Nor City and Feygard started to rise. He then proclaimed several prohibitions against the cult. They were no longer allowed to perform their rituals, and he tried to detain some of the priests. \n"
"Then he even banned the trade and use of heartsteel weapons as he feared they would be used to overthrow him.  He destroyed many weapons and confiscated others. Bonemeal potions were prohibited as well much to the disapproval of the smallfolk and the priests.\n"
"\n"
"[... here the story ends - you can't tell if there had been more pages ...]"
msgstr ""
"* de Wormath Splathershed * \n"
"\n"
"Fundatzione de su Regnu Ismentigadu (annu 2300)\n"
"Sos primos èsseres umanos, ghiados dae Arntuk su Poderosu, sunt bènnidos dae "
"su sud in tempos antigos e ant fundadu su Regnu Ismentigadu. Custa gente, "
"chi si naraiat Lethgar, at fraigadu bidditzolos in logos in ue como b'at "
"biddas e tzitades mannas. Nor City e Sullengard sunt istadas sas primas a "
"èssere fundadas.\n"
"Pustis de unu tempus, unos cantos esploradores sunt artziados a su Monte "
"Galmore, su monte prus artu de Dhayavar. Pro more de s'artària e de sa vista "
"meravigiosa, sos preìderos e sos magos issoro ant fraigadu unu santuàriu "
"acanta de sa punta, in ue istudiaiant sas artes màgicas e adoraiant sos deos "
"issoro. \n"
"\n"
"S'artziada de Kazaul (annu 2177)\n"
"Su magu macu e poderosu chi si naraiat Valugha fiat fissadu cun s'idea de "
"creare unu portale cara a un'àtera dimensione. Mancari sos cumpàngios magos "
"suos non fiant de acordu, est resèssidu a creare unu portale consumende "
"s'essèntzia vitale poderosa de sos frades suos e s'energia allogada in su "
"santuàriu. Su santuàriu est esplòdidu e unu barrancu mannu at isperradu in "
"duos su Monte Galmore. In su fundu suo s'est abertu su portale, chi luego "
"est istadu mutidu petzi 'S'Isperrada', e s'àrea devastada a inghìriu suo "
"'Undertell'. Su monte at fintzas betadu lava comente sàmbene chi essit dae "
"una ferida, e como est semper cobertu de fumu.\n"
"Dimònios e non-mortos de cada genia sunt essidos in su mundu passende dae su "
"portale, ghiados dae sos meres issoro, sos 'Kazaul'. Sos Kazaul etotu fiant "
"ghiados dae sos Meres Eternos, chi fiant àbiles meda in sas artes màgicas e "
"in s'arte de sa gherra. Luego sos mostros e sos meres issoro si sunt "
"ispartos in totu Dhayavar. Però, a pustis de unu tempus su portale est "
"istadu instàbile e a sa fine est rutu a pustis de unas cantas dècadas, ma su "
"dannu fiat giai fatu, ca mìgias de bèstias fiant giai passadas a cua dae "
"issu in su regnu. \n"
"B'est istada una gherra curtza e brutale. Cun sa pèrdida de belle totu sos "
"magos, sos Lethgar non teniant perunu podere contra a s'invasione de sos "
"mostros, e luego sunt istados derrotados e fatos iscraos dae sos Kazaul. Sos "
"Kazaul ant impostu su terrore in totu su Regnu Ismentigadu. Pariat chi nemos "
"esseret capatze de bìnchere sos Kazaul o de los cuntrastare, pro more de sa "
"fortza disumana issoro. \n"
"Tando sos Lethgar ant dèvidu fraigare tanas suta de terra pro sos opressores "
"issoro. Una tzitade manna est istada fraigada a inghìriu de su portale "
"istudadu e in sas grutas naturales suta de su Monte Galmore. Sunt istados "
"fraigados fintzas sa Turre de Carn e su Santuàriu in su Monte Abbaniedda, in "
"mesu de àteros bidditzolos de sos Kazaul suta de terra, chi non si podent "
"contare.\n"
"Mancari sa parte prus manna de sos Lethgar dispretziaret sos meres issoro, "
"unos cantos ant mustradu interessu pro sos rituales e pro sa majadoria "
"iscura de sos Kazaul. Gasi, sos Kha'zaan (devotos de sos Kazaul), una truma "
"de sighidores umanos de sos Kazaul, si sunt aunidos a inghìriu de sos meres "
"issoro e ant imparadu dae issos. Fiant impreados a s'ispissu pro fàghere "
"rispetare su domìniu brutale de sos Kazaul. Medas de sos mostros de oe sunt "
"formas de vida chi derivant dae esperimentos fatos in cussa època, comente "
"sos Izthiel, sos Gornaud, sos Wyrm, etc.\n"
"In cussu tempus, su Hira'zinn, su malu sinnale de sa gherra, at cumintzadu a "
"turmentare sa gente minuda. \n"
"\n"
"Sa Gherra de s'Arbèschida e s'artziada de Elythara e de s'Unione Elytharana "
"(annu 1537)\n"
"Una die, sos devotos elytharanos sunt arribados a s'oru de su mare de su "
"nord (su Mare de sas Làgrimas). Adoraiant sa lughe de Elythara, chi tzeguat "
"e chi purìficat. \n"
"Sos magos e sos gherreris elytharanos sunt resèssidos a bìnchere sos Kazaul "
"e sos Kha'zaan cun s'agiudu de sa lughe de Elythara, chi tzeguat, fùndida\n"
"\n"
"[... inoghe nch'ant istratzadu unas cantas pàginas ...]\n"
"\n"
"ant cumintzadu a fraigare sa tzitade de Feygard in s'oru de su Mare de sas "
"Làgrimas, chi luego s'est fata unu tzentru de cummèrtziu pro su regnu, pro "
"more de s'atzessu suo a su mare. \n"
"Est istada fundada sa bidda de Loneford, chi luego s'est fata famada pro sos "
"campos fèrtiles e pro sa birdura sana chi daiat a mandigare a sas partes de "
"su nord de su Regnu Ismentigadu. \n"
"Est istadu esploradu su Monte Abbaniedda, e in sa punta sua est istadu "
"fraigadu unu santuàriu mannu pro sos preìderos elytharanos, pro istudiare "
"s'arbèschida e s'iscurigada, su sole e sos isteddos, e pro vigilare su Regnu "
"Ismentigadu. Àteros santuàrios fiant in Feygard e in Nor City, e in cada "
"bidditzolu minore b'aiat unu tempieddu. Est istada fundada fintzas sa "
"colònia minerària de Prim, a pustis chi unos colonos ant agatadu suta de su "
"monte venas ricas de ferru e de carbone.\n"
"Sa tzitade de Fallhaven s'est fata unu tzentru de cummèrtziu chi "
"prosperaiat, pro more de sa positzione bona meda sua de rughe de caminos "
"intre su santuàriu de su Monte Abbaniedda, Stoutford, Nor City e Feygard. "
"Sunt istados fraigados magasinos mannos pro allogare in seguresa sas "
"mertzes. Però, sa richesa chi creschiat at luego atiradu trumas de ladros, "
"chi si sunt aunidos in un'organizatzione manna, su Grèmiu de sos Ladros, cun "
"sas sedes suas postas a cua in Fallhaven, in Feygard e in Nor City, chi "
"fiant sas tzitades prus ricas de cussu tempus. \n"
"In cussu tempus sunt istadas fundadas fintzas medas àteras biddas, comente "
"Brimhaven e Portu Lughente, e sunt istadas abertas sas minieras de Padente "
"Brusiadu.\n"
"Sas tzitades ant firmadu acordos de cummèrtziu pro fàghere prosperare de "
"prus su cummèrtziu. \n"
"\n"
"Fundatzione de su Regnu de Aewatha (annu 432)\n"
"Su cabu de sa famìlia prus importante de Nor City, Garthan I de sa casada "
"Houdart, s'est proclamadu Re, e cun custu at sinnadu sa fine de s'era "
"elytharana e su cumintzu de su regnu sustentadu dae s'Umbra. In cussu "
"momentu, su podere polìticu e su podere religiosu si sunt unidos a curtzu. "
"Prus su regnu prosperaiat, prus prosperaiat s'Umbra, e Elythara\n"
"\n"
"[... inoghe puru nch'ant istratzadu unas cantas pàginas ...]\n"
"\n"
"comente iscraos pro iscavare. In cussu tempus est istada fraigada fintzas sa "
"Presone de Pedralada, in ue sos traballadores chi fuiant dae su Monte "
"Galmore fiant postos in presone e lassados a si pudèschere. Però sas "
"minieras sunt istadas serradas a pustis de unos cantos annos pro more de sos "
"atacos frecuentes de sos mostros e de àteros orrores chi non si podent "
"nàrrere, chi biviant in s'iscuriu.\n"
"Remgard est istada fundada dae Korhald de Remgard e fraigada in un'ìsula "
"manna de su Lagu Laeroth. S'est fata famada pro s'arte de sos ferreris suos. "
"\n"
"Est istada fundada sa bidda de Crossglen, e bi sunt andados a bìvere "
"massajos.\n"
"Su Re Luthor est artziadu a su tronu comente erede diretu de su Re Oromir "
"III e at tramudadu sa capitale dae Nor City a Fallhaven, mentras su tzentru "
"de su cultu est abarradu in Nor City. Cando su Re Luthor s'est fatu prus "
"betzu, at intesu su bisòngiu de unu cussigeri, e gasi Lord Geomyr de Feygard "
"est istadu nominadu Manu de su Re. At fatu su dovere suo cun ossessione e "
"cun impignu mannu. \n"
"\n"
"Sas Gherras de sos Nòbiles (dae s'annu 25 a su 14)\n"
"Cando su Re Luthor est mortu, at lassadu su Regnu chene erede a su tronu. "
"Est istadu interradu in sas catacumbas suta de sa crèsia de Fallhaven. Su "
"chi est bènnidu a pustis, sas Gherras de sos Nòbiles, est istadu unu de sos "
"perìodos prus iscuros chi custu paisu apat mai bidu. \n"
"Si sunt formadas bator coalitziones, cada una guvernada dae unu Lord "
"poderosu. \n"
"Sa de otzidente fiat formada dae Stoutford e dae sos bidditzolos de su Monte "
"Abbaniedda, e fiat guvernada dae Lord Erwyn. \n"
"Sa de su nord fiat formada dae Feygard, Thalgard, Luthaven e Remgard, e fiat "
"guvernada dae Lord Geomyr. \n"
"Sa de oriente fiat formada dae Nor City, Sullengard, Portu Lughente e "
"Brimhaven, e fiat guvernada dae Lord Emeric. \n"
"S'àrea tzentrale de sa capitale, a su cumintzu, est abarrada neutrale e fiat "
"formada dae Fallhaven, Vilegard e Loneford (chi in antis fiant amministradas "
"dae su Re Luthor). \n"
"Sas Gherras de sos Nòbiles ant cumintzadu cando sos Sennores de sas terras "
"si sunt postos a brigare pro chie depiat èssere su Re nou, su legìtimu. \n"
"Sa prima pedra l'at betada Stoutford. Lord Erwyn at chircadu de aprofitare "
"de su tempus pro atacare s'àrea tzentrale, mentras sos àteros Lord fiant "
"impinnados a cuntierrare. Cheriat ocupare cussas terras pro controllare sas "
"àndalas de cummèrtziu cara a Nor City, pro tènnere s'influèntzia prus manna "
"e pro partzire sas àteras coalitziones. Fallhaven est istada distruida in "
"parte.\n"
"Sa vitòria de Erwyn est durada pagu, ca est istadu atacadu dae sa "
"coalitzione de oriente. Pro unos cantos annos, b'at àpidu medas batallas e "
"cumbatas minores chene contu pro su controllu de s'àrea tzentrale. Cando sos "
"duos Lord fiant debilitados, Lord Geomyr at atacadu e los at custrintos a "
"s'arrèndere. Est istadu firmadu su tratadu de paghe de Fallhaven e Lord "
"Geomyr est istadu proclamadu Re.\n"
"Su Hira'zinn at torradu a turmentare sas terras durante sa gherra. \n"
"\n"
"Su guvernu de su Re Geomyr (annu 14)\n"
"Su Re Geomyr at ispronadu sa gente a torrare a pesare sas tzitades "
"distruidas e a bogare sos rastros de sa gherra longa. At torradu a pònnere "
"unu sistema de tassas, e presìdios de sa Guàrdia Reale de Feygard in sa "
"parte prus manna de sas biddas. Geomyr at promòvidu su nepotismu e sa "
"corrutzione pro crèschere ancora de prus su podere suo.\n"
"Su cultu de s'Umbra s'est fatu semper prus importante pro sa gente minuda. "
"Sa gente de pòpulu at intesu su bisòngiu de èssere sarvada a pustis de su "
"perìodu duru de sas Gherras de sos Nòbiles, e at atzetadu s'Umbra comente "
"ghia cara a tempos mègius.\n"
"Lord Geomyr at cumintzadu a tìmere su podere de sa religione, e sas "
"tensiones intre Nor City e Feygard ant cumintzadu a crèschere. Tando at "
"proclamadu unas cantas proibitziones contra a su cultu. Sos devotos non "
"podiant prus fàghere sos rituales issoro, e at chircadu de arrestare unos "
"cantos de sos preìderos. \n"
"Pustis at proibidu fintzas su cummèrtziu e s'impreu de sas armas de atzàrgiu "
"de coro, ca timiat chi diant èssere impreadas pro lu derrocare.  At "
"distruidu medas armas e nd'at cunfiscadu àteras. Sunt istadas proibidas "
"fintzas sas potziones de farina de ossos, cun su disacordu mannu de sa gente "
"minuda e de sos preìderos.\n"
"\n"
"[... inoghe s'istòria acabbat - non si podet ischire si b'aiat àteras "
"pàginas ...]"

#: itemlist_brimhaven2.json:book_world_history_complete:description
msgid ""
"* by Wormath Splathershed * \n"
"\n"
"Foundation of the Forgotten Kingdom (year 2300)\n"
"The first humans, led by Arntuk the Mighty, came from the south in ancient times and established the Forgotten Kingdom. These people, called the Lethgar, built settlements at places where now great towns and cities are located. Nor City and Sullengard were the first to be founded.\n"
"Then some time later, a few explorers climbed Mount Galmore, the highest mountain in Dhayavar. Due to the elevation and marvelous view, their priests and mages built a sanctuary near the summit where they studied the arts of magic and worshipped their gods. \n"
"\n"
"Rise of Kazaul (year 2177)\n"
"The insane and powerful wizard called Valugha was obsessed with the notion of creating a portal to another plane. Even though his fellow mages disapproved, he was able to create a portal by consuming the powerful life essence of his brothers and the stored energy in the sanctuary. The sanctuary erupted in an explosion and a large ravine split Mt. Galmore apart. At its bottom, the portal opened, which was soon merely called the 'Rift', and the devastated area around it 'Undertell'. The mountain also spilled out lava like blood coming from a wound and is now clouded in smoke all the time.\n"
"All kinds of demons and undead emerged into the world through the portal, led by their masters, the 'Kazaul'. The Kazaul themselves were guided by the Eternal Masters who were incredibly skilled in magic and warcraft. Soon the monsters and their masters spread over whole of Dhayavar. However, the portal became unstable after a while and finally collapsed after several decades but the harm was already done as thousands of beasts had crept through it into the realm. \n"
"A short and brutal war was fought. With the loss of nearly all mages, the Lethgar were powerless against the monster invasion and were soon overthrown and enslaved by the Kazaul. The Kazaul imposed a reign of terror on the Forgotten Kingdom. It seemed no one was able to defeat or oppose the Kazaul due to their inhuman strength. \n"
"Then the Lethgar had to build underground lairs for their oppressors. A large city was built around the deactivated portal and in the natural caves under Mt. Galmore. Also, Carn Tower and the Sanctuary on Blackwater Mountain were built, among countless other underground Kazaul settlements.\n"
"Even though most Lethgar despised their masters, some showed interest in the rituals and dark sorcery of the Kazaul. As a result, the Kha'zaan (Kazaul cultists), a group of human Kazaul followers, gathered around their masters and learned from them. They were often used to enforce the brutal rule of the Kazaul. Many of the current monsters are living forms that evolved from experiments made during this era, such as Izthiels, Gornauds, Wyrms, etc.\n"
"By that time, the Hira'zinn, the omen of war, started plaguing the smallfolk. \n"
"\n"
"The War of Dawn and the Rise of Elythara and the Elytharan Union (year 1537)\n"
"One day, the Elytharan cultists arrived on the shore of the northern sea (Sea of Tears). They worshipped the blinding and cleansing light of Elythara. \n"
"The Elytharan mages and warriors were able to defeat the Kazaul and Kha'zaan with the help of the blinding light of Elythara which was forged into their weapons. The Kazaul were reduced to almost nothing because their Eternal Masters were slain. However Elythara and her cultists failed to completely annihilate them, as a few Kazaul and followers managed to hide in remote places in the total darkness, unknown to the Elytharans. This is because although the Kazaul's dark spells were powerless against the blinding light of Elythara, Elythara's power is diminished deep underground in the total darkness. Nevertheless, for hundreds of years the Kazaul hibernated in the darkness.  \n"
"The visual appearance of her powers, as well as her perceived benevolence towards the commoners lead to people to call her the Goddess of Light. People were overjoyed about the defeat of Kazaul.  The Elytharans helped the people organize life and built several towns and cities, dedicated to their goddess. Several aristocratic houses were formed by that time. Each city was ruled by one or two houses who closely collaborated with the Elytharan priests.\n"
"A long era of peace and prosperity followed and the Elytharan Union was founded, to spread the word of Elythara over the whole realm. Even though the aristocrats ruled the cities, people were mainly influenced by the Elytharan priests.\n"
"Obviously, the world under Elythara wasn't perfect, although that's what her priests wanted people to believe. Her 'light' was shown to those who refused to follow the 'right' way, generally leaving them blind or worse... \n"
"The Elytharans soon began erecting the city of Feygard on the shore of the Sea of Tears, which soon became a center of trade for the realm due to its access to the sea. \n"
"The town of Loneford was founded and it soon became famous for its fertile fields and healthy vegetable which fed the northern parts of the Forgotten Kingdom. \n"
"Blackwater Mountain was explored, and on its summit a large sanctuary for the Elytharan priests was erected to study dawn and dusk, the sun and stars, and to watch over the Forgotten Kingdom. Other sanctuaries were located in Feygard and Nor City, and shrines were found in each minor settlement. The mining colony of Prim was also founded after pioneers found rich sources of iron and coal under the mountain.\n"
"The city of Fallhaven became a prospering center of trade due to its excellent location as a junction between the sanctuary of Blackwater Mountain, Stoutford, Nor City and Feygard. Big storehouses were built to safely store shipments. However, bands of thieves were soon attracted by the growing wealth and united under one big organization, the Thieves' Guild, whose guild halls were secretly placed in Fallhaven, Feygard, and Nor City, those being the richest cities at that time. \n"
"Many other towns, including Brimhaven and Brightport were also founded around this time, and the Charwood mines were opened.\n"
"Trade agreements were signed between the cities in order to make trade prosper further. \n"
"\n"
"Establishment of the Aewatha Kingdom (year 432)\n"
"The head of the most important Nor City family, Garthan I of house Houdart, declared himself King, marking the end of the Elytharan era and the beginning of the Shadow-supported kingdom. At this point, political power and religious power became closely united. As the kingdom prospered, so did the Shadow, and Elythara was forgotten by almost everyone in only a handful of generations. A large temple complex with a magnificent cathedral was built in the center of Nor City where the former shrines of Elythara had been located. Smaller churches were built across the country. People now commonly believed in the Shadow.\n"
"Garthan I ordered the exploration of the dreaded Mt. Galmore and a large mine was opened for a few decades where gems and gold were found in abundance.  Any remaining Elytharan followers were used as slaves for the digging. At that time the Flagstone Prison was also built, where runaway workers from Mt. Galmore were imprisoned and were left to rot. However the mines were closed after some years due to frequent monster attacks and other unspeakable horrors who dwelt in the dark.\n"
"Remgard was founded by Korhald of Remgard and built on a large island in Lake Laeroth. It became famous for its excellent smithing services. \n"
"The village of Crossglen was founded, and farmers settled there.\n"
"King Luthor ascended to the throne as the direct heir of King Oromir III and moved the capital from Nor City to Fallhaven, while the center of worship remained in Nor City. As King Luthor got older he felt the need for an advisor, and so Lord Geomyr of Feygard was named Hand of the King. He fulfilled his duty with great obsession and effort. \n"
"\n"
"The Noble Wars (year 25 to 14)\n"
"When King Luthor died, he left the Kingdom with no heir to the throne. He was buried in the catacombs under Fallhaven church. What followed, the Noble Wars, was one of the darkest periods this country has witnessed. \n"
"Four coalitions were formed which were each ruled by one powerful Lord. \n"
"The Western one consisted of Stoutford and the settlements on Blackwater Mountain, and was ruled by Lord Erwyn. \n"
"The Northern one consisted of Feygard, Thalgard, Luthaven and Remgard, and was ruled by Lord Geomyr. \n"
"The Eastern one consisted of Nor City, Sullengard, Brightport and Brimhaven, and was ruled by Lord Emeric. \n"
"The center capital area at first remained neutral and consisted of Fallhaven, Vilegard and Loneford (formerly administrated by King Luthor). \n"
"The Noble Wars started with the Landlords arguing about who was to be the new, legitimate, King. \n"
"The first stone was thrown by Stoutford. Lord Erwyn tried to use the time to attack the center area when the other Lords were busy debating. He wanted to occupy those to control the trade routes to Nor City, to gain the largest influence and to fracture other coalitions. Fallhaven was partially destroyed.\n"
"Erwyn's success was a short one, as he was attacked by the Eastern coalition. For several years, numerous battles and countless skirmishes were fought over control of the center area. When both Lords were weakened, Lord Geomyr attacked and forced both to surrender. The peace treaty of Fallhaven was signed and Lord Geomyr was proclaimed King.\n"
"The Hira'zinn haunted the lands once again during the war. \n"
"\n"
"The Rule of King Geomyr (year 14)\n"
"King Geomyr urged people to restore the destroyed cities and remove the traces of the long war. He reinstated a tax system, and garrisons of the Royal Guard of Feygard, to most of the villages. Geomyr promoted nepotism and corruption to further increase his power.\n"
"The cult of the Shadow became ever more important for the smallfolk. The commoners felt the need for salvation after the harsh period of the Noble Wars and accepted the Shadow as their guide into better times.\n"
"Lord Geomyr became fearful of the power of the religion and tensions between Nor City and Feygard started to rise. He then proclaimed several prohibitions against the cult. They were no longer allowed to perform their rituals, and he tried to detain some of the priests. \n"
"Then he even banned the trade and use of heartsteel weapons as he feared they would be used to overthrow him.  He destroyed many weapons and confiscated others. Bonemeal potions were prohibited as well much to the disapproval of the smallfolk and the priests."
msgstr ""
"* de Wormath Splathershed * \n"
"\n"
"Fundatzione de su Regnu Ismentigadu (annu 2300)\n"
"Sos primos èsseres umanos, ghiados dae Arntuk su Poderosu, sunt bènnidos dae "
"su sud in tempos antigos e ant fundadu su Regnu Ismentigadu. Custa gente, "
"chi si naraiat Lethgar, at fraigadu bidditzolos in logos in ue como b'at "
"biddas e tzitades mannas. Nor City e Sullengard sunt istadas sas primas a "
"èssere fundadas.\n"
"Pustis de unu tempus, unos cantos esploradores sunt artziados a su Monte "
"Galmore, su monte prus artu de Dhayavar. Pro more de s'artària e de sa vista "
"meravigiosa, sos preìderos e sos magos issoro ant fraigadu unu santuàriu "
"acanta de sa punta, in ue istudiaiant sas artes màgicas e adoraiant sos deos "
"issoro. \n"
"\n"
"S'artziada de Kazaul (annu 2177)\n"
"Su magu macu e poderosu chi si naraiat Valugha fiat fissadu cun s'idea de "
"creare unu portale cara a un'àtera dimensione. Mancari sos cumpàngios magos "
"suos non fiant de acordu, est resèssidu a creare unu portale consumende "
"s'essèntzia vitale poderosa de sos frades suos e s'energia allogada in su "
"santuàriu. Su santuàriu est esplòdidu e unu barrancu mannu at isperradu in "
"duos su Monte Galmore. In su fundu suo s'est abertu su portale, chi luego "
"est istadu mutidu petzi 'S'Isperrada', e s'àrea devastada a inghìriu suo "
"'Undertell'. Su monte at fintzas betadu lava comente sàmbene chi essit dae "
"una ferida, e como est semper cobertu de fumu.\n"
"Dimònios e non-mortos de cada genia sunt essidos in su mundu passende dae su "
"portale, ghiados dae sos meres issoro, sos 'Kazaul'. Sos Kazaul etotu fiant "
"ghiados dae sos Meres Eternos, chi fiant àbiles meda in sas artes màgicas e "
"in s'arte de sa gherra. Luego sos mostros e sos meres issoro si sunt "
"ispartos in totu Dhayavar. Però, a pustis de unu tempus su portale est "
"istadu instàbile e a sa fine est rutu a pustis de unas cantas dècadas, ma su "
"dannu fiat giai fatu, ca mìgias de bèstias fiant giai passadas a cua dae "
"issu in su regnu. \n"
"B'est istada una gherra curtza e brutale. Cun sa pèrdida de belle totu sos "
"magos, sos Lethgar non teniant perunu podere contra a s'invasione de sos "
"mostros, e luego sunt istados derrotados e fatos iscraos dae sos Kazaul. Sos "
"Kazaul ant impostu su terrore in totu su Regnu Ismentigadu. Pariat chi nemos "
"esseret capatze de bìnchere sos Kazaul o de los cuntrastare, pro more de sa "
"fortza disumana issoro. \n"
"Tando sos Lethgar ant dèvidu fraigare tanas suta de terra pro sos opressores "
"issoro. Una tzitade manna est istada fraigada a inghìriu de su portale "
"istudadu e in sas grutas naturales suta de su Monte Galmore. Sunt istados "
"fraigados fintzas sa Turre de Carn e su Santuàriu in su Monte Abbaniedda, in "
"mesu de àteros bidditzolos de sos Kazaul suta de terra, chi non si podent "
"contare.\n"
"Mancari sa parte prus manna de sos Lethgar dispretziaret sos meres issoro, "
"unos cantos ant mustradu interessu pro sos rituales e pro sa majadoria "
"iscura de sos Kazaul. Gasi, sos Kha'zaan (devotos de sos Kazaul), una truma "
"de sighidores umanos de sos Kazaul, si sunt aunidos a inghìriu de sos meres "
"issoro e ant imparadu dae issos. Fiant impreados a s'ispissu pro fàghere "
"rispetare su domìniu brutale de sos Kazaul. Medas de sos mostros de oe sunt "
"formas de vida chi derivant dae esperimentos fatos in cussa època, comente "
"sos Izthiel, sos Gornaud, sos Wyrm, etc.\n"
"In cussu tempus, su Hira'zinn, su malu sinnale de sa gherra, at cumintzadu a "
"turmentare sa gente minuda. \n"
"\n"
"Sa Gherra de s'Arbèschida e s'artziada de Elythara e de s'Unione Elytharana "
"(annu 1537)\n"
"Una die, sos devotos elytharanos sunt arribados a s'oru de su mare de su "
"nord (su Mare de sas Làgrimas). Adoraiant sa lughe de Elythara, chi tzeguat "
"e chi purìficat. \n"
"Sos magos e sos gherreris elytharanos sunt resèssidos a bìnchere sos Kazaul "
"e sos Kha'zaan cun s'agiudu de sa lughe de Elythara, chi tzeguat, fùndida in "
"sas armas issoro. Sos Kazaul sunt istados reduidos a belle nudda, ca sos "
"Meres Eternos issoro fiant istados mortos. Però Elythara e sos devotos suos "
"non sunt resèssidos a los distrùere de su totu, ca unos cantos Kazaul e "
"sighidores issoro sunt resèssidos a si cuare in logos remotos, in s'iscuriu "
"prus totale, chi sos elytharanos non connoschiant. Custu ca, mancari sos "
"incantos iscuros de sos Kazaul non tennerent perunu podere contra a sa lughe "
"de Elythara, chi tzeguat, su podere de Elythara si mìnimat in sas "
"profundidades de sa terra, in s'iscuriu prus totale. Su matessi, pro "
"chèntinas de annos sos Kazaul sunt abarrados in letargu in s'iscuriu.  \n"
"S'aspetu visìbile de sos poderes suos, e fintzas sa bonidade chi sa gente de "
"pòpulu bidiat in issa, ant fatu chi sa gente la mutiret Dea de sa Lughe. Sa "
"gente fiat prena de allegria pro sa derrota de Kazaul.  Sos elytharanos ant "
"agiudadu sa gente a organizare sa vida e ant fraigadu medas biddas e "
"tzitades, dedicadas a sa dea issoro. In cussu tempus si sunt formadas unas "
"cantas casadas aristocràticas. Cada tzitade fiat guvernada dae una o duas "
"casadas, chi collaboraiant a curtzu cun sos preìderos elytharanos.\n"
"A pustis est bènnida un'era longa de paghe e de prosperidade, e est istada "
"fundada s'Unione Elytharana, pro ispàrghere sa paràula de Elythara in totu "
"su regnu. Mancari sos nòbiles guvernarent sas tzitades, sa gente fiat "
"influentzada mescamente dae sos preìderos elytharanos.\n"
"Est craru chi su mundu suta de Elythara non fiat perfetu, mancari sos "
"preìderos suos cheriant chi sa gente pensaret gasi. Sa 'lughe' sua fiat "
"mustrada a chie refudaiat de sighire su caminu 'giustu', e in generale los "
"lassaiat tzegos o peus... \n"
"Luego sos elytharanos ant cumintzadu a fraigare sa tzitade de Feygard in "
"s'oru de su Mare de sas Làgrimas, chi luego s'est fata unu tzentru de "
"cummèrtziu pro su regnu, pro more de s'atzessu suo a su mare. \n"
"Est istada fundada sa bidda de Loneford, chi luego s'est fata famada pro sos "
"campos fèrtiles e pro sa birdura sana chi daiat a mandigare a sas partes de "
"su nord de su Regnu Ismentigadu. \n"
"Est istadu esploradu su Monte Abbaniedda, e in sa punta sua est istadu "
"fraigadu unu santuàriu mannu pro sos preìderos elytharanos, pro istudiare "
"s'arbèschida e s'iscurigada, su sole e sos isteddos, e pro vigilare su Regnu "
"Ismentigadu. Àteros santuàrios fiant in Feygard e in Nor City, e in cada "
"bidditzolu minore b'aiat unu tempieddu. Est istada fundada fintzas sa "
"colònia minerària de Prim, a pustis chi unos colonos ant agatadu suta de su "
"monte venas ricas de ferru e de carbone.\n"
"Sa tzitade de Fallhaven s'est fata unu tzentru de cummèrtziu chi "
"prosperaiat, pro more de sa positzione bona meda sua de rughe de caminos "
"intre su santuàriu de su Monte Abbaniedda, Stoutford, Nor City e Feygard. "
"Sunt istados fraigados magasinos mannos pro allogare in seguresa sas "
"mertzes. Però, sa richesa chi creschiat at luego atiradu trumas de ladros, "
"chi si sunt aunidos in un'organizatzione manna, su Grèmiu de sos Ladros, cun "
"sas sedes suas postas a cua in Fallhaven, in Feygard e in Nor City, chi "
"fiant sas tzitades prus ricas de cussu tempus. \n"
"In cussu tempus sunt istadas fundadas fintzas medas àteras biddas, comente "
"Brimhaven e Portu Lughente, e sunt istadas abertas sas minieras de Padente "
"Brusiadu.\n"
"Sas tzitades ant firmadu acordos de cummèrtziu pro fàghere prosperare de "
"prus su cummèrtziu. \n"
"\n"
"Fundatzione de su Regnu de Aewatha (annu 432)\n"
"Su cabu de sa famìlia prus importante de Nor City, Garthan I de sa casada "
"Houdart, s'est proclamadu Re, e cun custu at sinnadu sa fine de s'era "
"elytharana e su cumintzu de su regnu sustentadu dae s'Umbra. In cussu "
"momentu, su podere polìticu e su podere religiosu si sunt unidos a curtzu. "
"Prus su regnu prosperaiat, prus prosperaiat s'Umbra, e Elythara est istada "
"ismentigada dae belle totus in pagas generatziones. In su tzentru de Nor "
"City, in ue b'aiat àpidu sos santuàrios antigos de Elythara, est istadu "
"fraigadu unu cumplessu mannu de tèmpios cun una catedrale meravigiosa. In "
"totu su paisu sunt istadas fraigadas crèsias prus piticas. Como sa gente, in "
"generale, creiat in s'Umbra.\n"
"Garthan I at ordinadu de esplorare su Monte Galmore, chi totus timiant, e "
"pro unas cantas dècadas est istada aberta una miniera manna in ue ant "
"agatadu gemmas e oro in abbundàntzia.  Sos sighidores elytharanos chi fiant "
"ancora abarrados sunt istados impreados comente iscraos pro iscavare. In "
"cussu tempus est istada fraigada fintzas sa Presone de Pedralada, in ue sos "
"traballadores chi fuiant dae su Monte Galmore fiant postos in presone e "
"lassados a si pudèschere. Però sas minieras sunt istadas serradas a pustis "
"de unos cantos annos pro more de sos atacos frecuentes de sos mostros e de "
"àteros orrores chi non si podent nàrrere, chi biviant in s'iscuriu.\n"
"Remgard est istada fundada dae Korhald de Remgard e fraigada in un'ìsula "
"manna de su Lagu Laeroth. S'est fata famada pro s'arte de sos ferreris suos. "
"\n"
"Est istada fundada sa bidda de Crossglen, e bi sunt andados a bìvere "
"massajos.\n"
"Su Re Luthor est artziadu a su tronu comente erede diretu de su Re Oromir "
"III e at tramudadu sa capitale dae Nor City a Fallhaven, mentras su tzentru "
"de su cultu est abarradu in Nor City. Cando su Re Luthor s'est fatu prus "
"betzu, at intesu su bisòngiu de unu cussigeri, e gasi Lord Geomyr de Feygard "
"est istadu nominadu Manu de su Re. At fatu su dovere suo cun ossessione e "
"cun impignu mannu. \n"
"\n"
"Sas Gherras de sos Nòbiles (dae s'annu 25 a su 14)\n"
"Cando su Re Luthor est mortu, at lassadu su Regnu chene erede a su tronu. "
"Est istadu interradu in sas catacumbas suta de sa crèsia de Fallhaven. Su "
"chi est bènnidu a pustis, sas Gherras de sos Nòbiles, est istadu unu de sos "
"perìodos prus iscuros chi custu paisu apat mai bidu. \n"
"Si sunt formadas bator coalitziones, cada una guvernada dae unu Lord "
"poderosu. \n"
"Sa de otzidente fiat formada dae Stoutford e dae sos bidditzolos de su Monte "
"Abbaniedda, e fiat guvernada dae Lord Erwyn. \n"
"Sa de su nord fiat formada dae Feygard, Thalgard, Luthaven e Remgard, e fiat "
"guvernada dae Lord Geomyr. \n"
"Sa de oriente fiat formada dae Nor City, Sullengard, Portu Lughente e "
"Brimhaven, e fiat guvernada dae Lord Emeric. \n"
"S'àrea tzentrale de sa capitale, a su cumintzu, est abarrada neutrale e fiat "
"formada dae Fallhaven, Vilegard e Loneford (chi in antis fiant amministradas "
"dae su Re Luthor). \n"
"Sas Gherras de sos Nòbiles ant cumintzadu cando sos Sennores de sas terras "
"si sunt postos a brigare pro chie depiat èssere su Re nou, su legìtimu. \n"
"Sa prima pedra l'at betada Stoutford. Lord Erwyn at chircadu de aprofitare "
"de su tempus pro atacare s'àrea tzentrale, mentras sos àteros Lord fiant "
"impinnados a cuntierrare. Cheriat ocupare cussas terras pro controllare sas "
"àndalas de cummèrtziu cara a Nor City, pro tènnere s'influèntzia prus manna "
"e pro partzire sas àteras coalitziones. Fallhaven est istada distruida in "
"parte.\n"
"Sa vitòria de Erwyn est durada pagu, ca est istadu atacadu dae sa "
"coalitzione de oriente. Pro unos cantos annos, b'at àpidu medas batallas e "
"cumbatas minores chene contu pro su controllu de s'àrea tzentrale. Cando sos "
"duos Lord fiant debilitados, Lord Geomyr at atacadu e los at custrintos a "
"s'arrèndere. Est istadu firmadu su tratadu de paghe de Fallhaven e Lord "
"Geomyr est istadu proclamadu Re.\n"
"Su Hira'zinn at torradu a turmentare sas terras durante sa gherra. \n"
"\n"
"Su guvernu de su Re Geomyr (annu 14)\n"
"Su Re Geomyr at ispronadu sa gente a torrare a pesare sas tzitades "
"distruidas e a bogare sos rastros de sa gherra longa. At torradu a pònnere "
"unu sistema de tassas, e presìdios de sa Guàrdia Reale de Feygard in sa "
"parte prus manna de sas biddas. Geomyr at promòvidu su nepotismu e sa "
"corrutzione pro crèschere ancora de prus su podere suo.\n"
"Su cultu de s'Umbra s'est fatu semper prus importante pro sa gente minuda. "
"Sa gente de pòpulu at intesu su bisòngiu de èssere sarvada a pustis de su "
"perìodu duru de sas Gherras de sos Nòbiles, e at atzetadu s'Umbra comente "
"ghia cara a tempos mègius.\n"
"Lord Geomyr at cumintzadu a tìmere su podere de sa religione, e sas "
"tensiones intre Nor City e Feygard ant cumintzadu a crèschere. Tando at "
"proclamadu unas cantas proibitziones contra a su cultu. Sos devotos non "
"podiant prus fàghere sos rituales issoro, e at chircadu de arrestare unos "
"cantos de sos preìderos. \n"
"Pustis at proibidu fintzas su cummèrtziu e s'impreu de sas armas de atzàrgiu "
"de coro, ca timiat chi diant èssere impreadas pro lu derrocare.  At "
"distruidu medas armas e nd'at cunfiscadu àteras. Sunt istadas proibidas "
"fintzas sas potziones de farina de ossos, cun su disacordu mannu de sa gente "
"minuda e de sos preìderos."

