#: itemlist_brightport.json:brightport_book
msgid "The Noble Wars"
msgstr "Sas Gherras de sos Nòbiles"

#: itemlist_brightport.json:brightport_book:description
msgid "In the year 57 of the rule of King luthor, the era of prosperity came to an end. Our king and hero, died. The lords, dukes, and nobles gathered in the capital of Fallhaven. To attend the funerary process of the king. At the time Fallhaven was a great city, extending it's reach much farther. Not long after, the nobility found themselves at an impasse, who would become the next ruler? King Luthor had left behind no known heir, and the opinions of the nobles shifted amongst themselves. One side pushed for Lord Erwin of House Garland as the new king, The ruler of Stoutford. Stoutford had long been the military center of the kingdom, experienced and hardened in their clashes with the uncivilized tribes of the western bogs and wildlands, as well as the occasional demonic incursions of Undertell. The warriors of Stoutford were a formidable force, the cornerstone of the kingdom's defense. Many nobles disagreed with House Garland ruling and instead favored Lord Emeric of House Houdart, the ruling house of Nor City which was the kingdom's historical capital and the center of culture and worship of the Shadow. The third faction rallied around Lord Geomyr of House Aumwill, the lord of Feygard and the former king's advisor. Lastly, a final faction was formed by the nobles of the central lands, who at first remained neutral, but fearing that a new king might threaten the status of Fallhaven as capital and shift it's importance away, chose to oppose the others. As discussions progressed, the four factions soon solidified into four coalitions. The Western Coalition, formed by Lord Erwin and his vassals, was centered around the town of Stoutford, along with it were the town of Prim and the settlement of Blackwater Mountain. The Central Coalition was formed by the various nobility and burghers of Crossglen, Loneford, Fallhaven, Vilegard, and Charwood. The Eastern Coalition was formed by the 3 great houses of Nor City with Lord Emeric of House Houdart in charge, along with other more minor nobility, especially those of Brimhaven and Brightport. And the clergy of Sullengard, who sought to return the king back to the historical center of Shadow worship. Lastly, the Northern Coalition, led by Lord Geomyr, was comprised of the city of Feygard, which housed the loathed cult of Elythara, as well as the mountain settlement of Thalgard and the town of Remgard. With this, the sides were set. As the discussions stalled, what was at first whispers turned to shouts of command. Lord Erwin rallied his troops to be the one first to move towards the central lands, the spies of the various factions rode their horses in a hurry to announce their overlords. By the time news reached the East, the Western troops were on the move. The western troops split in 3 and rallied in all directions. North, towards Loneford, south towards Sullengard, and northeast towards the capital. The 1st army had met no resistance taking Crossglen, and the occupation of the village was relatively peaceful until the end of the conflicts. In Fallhaven, the nobles, lacking central leadership, hurriedly mustered a militia force to man the palisades and resist the western coalition, having managed to do so just in time to offer resistance. Meanwhile, the 3rd army, moving south, struggled to cross the Sutdover River, delaying their advance on Sullengard. The houses of Nor City were caught off guard; no one had assumed the conflict would begin so soon after the discussions stalled. They rallied their troops, the bulk of their forces being comprised of commoners and numerous levies. The members of house Houdart led the army, with the trained knights of its branching houses forming the elite core of their forces. Orders were sent to the regional leadership, and the armies moved to meet with their allies. The 1st army was led by Lord Emeric of Imeria Houdart The 2nd army was led by Duke Vergas of Ryfarion Houdart, and the 3rd army was led by Baron Benzimos of Worgand Houdart. Ensuring the house of Houdart and it's branches would lead the Kingdom if they were to succeed. Lord Emeric moved his army towards Fallhaven right as the attack of the Western Coalition commenced, deceptive correspondence painted himself to the central nobles as reinforcements. Making the towns of Vilegard and Charwood join in with the eastern coalition. The second army merged with the troops of Brightport, while the third moved south to defend Sullengard. And so it commenced, the start of the First Noble War. The troops of the western coalition advanced to the crossroads fortification, capturing it with minor resistance. Scouts were sent south and north to gauge the other coalition's approach, as the bulk of the troops moved towards the defenseless Loneford. In the south, the Western forces had passed the river and were on the eastern bank, moving towards Sullengard. In the center, Stoutford's elite forces crushed the meager militia and forcefully assimilated the town guard into their ranks, just in time, as Lord Emeric and his troops approached from the east. The Battle of Fallhaven began. Bodies fell on each side. Stoutford's hardened elite barely held on against the numerous forces of Nor City. Fallhaven burned, its inhabitants forced to hide or flee. Its wealthier citizens had already escaped to Feygard, taking their possessions with them. In the south, the troops of the western coalition met with the forces of the eastern coalition, led by Baron Benzimos. The two armies clashed, and the Western Coalition was on its back foot. With their back against the river, they opted for a retreat. Hoping to form a defensive line at the bridge and defend Stoutford's southern flank. The leaders, whose names were lost to history, hastily pulled back, whilst suffering many casualties. the plan to capture Sullengard having failed. To the north, Stoutford's troops secured Loneford with ease. Scouts reported no movement from the northern coalition. Lord Emeric's central forces soon moved to contest the crossroads, leading to skirmishes along the Duleian Road. Meanwhile, the Eastern Coalition's army, led by Duke Vergas, wary of Feygard's movements, sent scouts north to assess the Northern Coalition's response as their forces moved to merge with Brimhaven's forces. This predicament continued for many years. Battles devolved into minor skirmishes as both coalitions avoided any decisive engagements, unwilling to risk the lives of their troops. Both sides camped outside the ever-burning ruins of Fallhaven. In the south, the Sutdover River became the dividing line, while in the north, skirmishes were taking place in the forest between Brimhaven and Loneford. The Northern Coalition having made no move. The prolonged stalemate created a false sense of security. The garrisons of the encampments set to protect the northern flanks of both coalitions steadily diminished as the main forces required reinforcements to replenish their ranks. An uneasy truce took hold, allowing each side time to recover for a decisive battle. The war exposed the strengths and weaknesses of both sides. The Eastern Coalition, backed by Nor City, wielded immense wealth and manpower but it was stretched thin, its forces spread too far apart. The Western Coalition could afford to fight the larger forces of the East due due to their position and their proximity to the coalition's center of power in Stoutford. Manpower being the only issue, but the West employed prisoners from the mines as footmen, with its elite group of warriors being able to turn a disadvantage of numbers into an equal fight. With this in mind, Lord Emeric devised a plan. He wanted to capture Fallhaven and secure the symbol of the king from the former king Luthor's grave. He would draw away Erwin's reinforcements in Fallhaven via an attack from the south and then attack the Western Coalition in Fallhaven. The period of the Second War commenced. The East reinforced its southern army led by Baron Benzimos, ordering him to attack the bridge and take it at all costs. This plan succeeded, leading to a panic in the center of the Western troops. The ruins of Fallhaven, now a smoldering ground far from its marble clad roads and opulent buildings. were contested by skirmishes nearly every day. The reinforcements from Stoutford and Blackwater allowed the Western coalition to hold its line, but the sudden advance from the south required that the supply of recruits was to focus on the Sutdover. Having moved according to the Eastern Coalition's plan, Lord Emeric rallied his troops. The Second Battle of Fallhaven commenced. Larger and more brutal than the first, having fought for months on end, both sides lost hundreds of troops. Lord Emeric's forces, having seemingly bested their enemies, started advancing towards the west. At that same time, the expected happened. The Third period of the Noble Warsb began. The troops of Feygard suddenly moved south from Feygard and Thalgard, crushing the minor garrisons set to defend against the north and moved to capture Loneford and Brimhaven. In Brimhaven, the leadership panicked and switched sides, leaving a portion of the Eastern troops led by Duke Vergas to follow Brimhaven in their rebellion and switch sides. The loyal to Nor City Vergas, fled along with the remaining of his troops to Brightport. Loneford was swiftly captured, and the advance of the northern coalition to Fallhaven was imminent. The Eastern Coalition was the first to disengage, with the forces of Baron Benzimos retreating to the stronghold of Sullengard. The remaining troops of Lord Emeric moved southeast on the Duleian. Lord Geomyr split his forces in two: one chased after Lord Emeric's army, while the other moved to capture the remains of Fallhaven. In Brightport, The Feygardian troops met the resistance hastily mounted by the remaining troops of Duke Vergas, and were successful in routing them, securing Brightport. Feygard captured Fallhaven and Crossglen, then moved toward Stoutford, where the western coalition prepared for a siege. Feygard's troops caught up to the fleeing troops of the Eastern coalition and dealt a devastating blow to the exhausted forces. Baron Benzimos left a small contingent to defend Sullengard and moved to assist his lord in the Battle of the now cursed forest. The Blackwater settlements were bribed to cut their support of the Western Coalition; their leaders were spared. The Feygardians, laid siege to Stoutford, capturing Lord Erwin and executing him, along with the surviving members of House Garland. The decisive battle between the troops of Feygard and the Eastern coalition, ended with Baron Benzimos recklessly charging into the ranks of armored Feygard knights. Leading to his demise. lord Emeric was killed by a stray arrow, and only a third of the troops returned to Nor City. House Welfort took control and signed a treaty with Feygard. Lord Geomyr was crowned king, marking the end of the war."
msgstr ""
"In s'annu 57 de su regnu de su Re Luthor, s'època de sa prosperidade est "
"acabbada. Su re e eroe nostru est mortu. Sos sennores, sos ducas e sos "
"nòbiles si sunt aunidos in sa capitale, Fallhaven, pro assistire a su "
"funerale de su re. In cussu tempus Fallhaven fiat una tzitade manna, chi "
"s'allargaiat meda de prus. Pagu tempus a pustis, sos nòbiles si sunt "
"agatados in unu puntu mortu: chie diat èssere istadu su guvernadore nou? Su "
"Re Luthor no aiat lassadu perunu erede connotu, e sas opiniones de sos "
"nòbiles cambiaiant intre issos. Una parte ispinghiat pro Lord Erwin de sa "
"casada Garland comente re nou, su guvernadore de Stoutford. Stoutford fiat "
"istada dae tempus meda su tzentru militare de su regnu, esperta e intostada "
"in sos iscontros cun sas tribùs agrestes de sas paules e de sos sartos de "
"otzidente, e fintzas in sas incursiones de sos dimònios chi dae cando in "
"cando arribaiant dae Undertell. Sos gherreris de Stoutford fiant una fortza "
"formidàbile, sa pedra angulare de sa defensa de su regnu. Medas nòbiles non "
"fiant de acordu cun su guvernu de sa casada Garland e preferiant imbetzes a "
"Lord Emeric de sa casada Houdart, sa casada chi guvernaiat Nor City, chi "
"fiat sa capitale istòrica de su regnu e su tzentru de sa cultura e de su "
"cultu de s'Umbra. Sa de tres fatziones s'est aunida a inghìriu de Lord "
"Geomyr de sa casada Aumwill, su sennore de Feygard e cussigeri de su re "
"mortu. A sa fine, un'ùrtima fatzione l'ant formada sos nòbiles de sas terras "
"tzentrales, chi a su cumintzu sunt abarrados neutrales, ma, timende chi unu "
"re nou diat pòdere minetzare su status de Fallhaven comente capitale e nde "
"diat pòdere bogare s'importàntzia, ant seberadu de si opònnere a sos àteros. "
"Andende a in antis sas discussiones, sas bator fatziones si sunt luego fatas "
"bator coalitziones. Sa Coalitzione de Otzidente, formada dae Lord Erwin e "
"dae sos vassallos suos, teniat su tzentru in sa bidda de Stoutford, e cun "
"issa b'aiat sa bidda de Prim e su bidditzolu de su Monte Abbaniedda. Sa "
"Coalitzione de su Tzentru fiat formada dae sos nòbiles e dae sos burghesos "
"de Crossglen, Loneford, Fallhaven, Vilegard e Padente Brusiadu. Sa "
"Coalitzione de Oriente fiat formada dae sas 3 casadas mannas de Nor City, "
"ghiadas dae Lord Emeric de sa casada Houdart, cun àteros nòbiles minores, "
"mescamente cussos de Brimhaven e de Portu Lughente. E cun su cleru de "
"Sullengard, chi cheriat torrare su re a su tzentru istòricu de su cultu de "
"s'Umbra. A s'urtimada, sa Coalitzione de su Nord, ghiada dae Lord Geomyr, "
"cumprendiat sa tzitade de Feygard, chi daiat allogu a su cultu odiadu de "
"Elythara, e fintzas su bidditzolu de monte de Thalgard e sa bidda de "
"Remgard. Gasi, sas partes fiant postas. Cando sas discussiones si sunt "
"firmadas, su chi a su cumintzu fiant murmutos s'est fatu boghes de cumandu. "
"Lord Erwin at aunidu sas tropas suas pro èssere su primu a si mòvere cara a "
"sas terras tzentrales, e sas ispias de sas fatziones diferentes sunt "
"cùrridas a caddu, cun presse, pro avisare sos sennores issoro. Cando sa nova "
"est arribada a Oriente, sas tropas de Otzidente fiant giai in caminu. Sas "
"tropas de otzidente si sunt partzidas in 3 e sunt andadas in totu sas "
"diretziones: a nord, cara a Loneford, a sud, cara a Sullengard, e a nord-"
"est, cara a sa capitale. Su de 1 esèrtzitu no at agatadu peruna resistèntzia "
"leende Crossglen, e s'ocupatzione de sa bidda est istada bastante in paghe "
"finas a sa fine de sos cunflitos. In Fallhaven, sos nòbiles, chene una ghia "
"tzentrale, ant aunidu de presse una milìtzia pro presidiare sas palitzadas e "
"pro resìstere a sa coalitzione de otzidente, e bi sunt resèssidos giustu in "
"tempus pro fàghere resistèntzia. In su matessi tempus, su de 3 esèrtzitu, "
"chi andaiat a sud, at àpidu dificultades a passare su Riu Sutdover, e custu "
"at ritardadu s'avantzada sua cara a Sullengard. Sas casadas de Nor City sunt "
"istadas leadas a s'ispessada; nemos aiat pensadu chi su cunflitu diat "
"cumintzare gasi luego a pustis chi sas discussiones si fiant firmadas. Ant "
"aunidu sas tropas issoro, e sa parte prus manna de sas fortzas fiat formada "
"dae gente de pòpulu e dae medas sordados noos. Sos membros de sa casada "
"Houdart ghiaiant s'esèrtzitu, e sos cavalieris espertos de sas casadas chi "
"derivaiant dae issa formaiant su nùcleu de èlite de sas fortzas. Sunt "
"istados mandados sos òrdines a sos cabos regionales, e sos esèrtzitos si "
"sunt mòvidos pro s'aunire cun sos alleados issoro. Su de 1 esèrtzitu fiat "
"ghiadu dae Lord Emeric de Imeria Houdart. Su de 2 esèrtzitu fiat ghiadu dae "
"su Duca Vergas de Ryfarion Houdart, e su de 3 esèrtzitu dae su Barone "
"Benzimos de Worgand Houdart. Gasi si fiant assegurados chi sa casada de "
"Houdart e sos ramos suos diant ghiare su Regnu si esserent bintos. Lord "
"Emeric at mòvidu s'esèrtzitu suo cara a Fallhaven pròpiu cando cumintzaiat "
"s'atacu de sa Coalitzione de Otzidente, e cun lìteras ingannosas s'est "
"presentadu a sos nòbiles de su tzentru comente rinfortzu. Gasi sas biddas de "
"Vilegard e de Padente Brusiadu si sunt aunidas a sa coalitzione de oriente. "
"Su de 2 esèrtzitu s'est aunidu cun sas tropas de Portu Lughente, mentras su "
"de 3 est faladu a sud pro difèndere Sullengard. E gasi at cumintzadu sa "
"Prima Gherra de sos Nòbiles. Sas tropas de sa coalitzione de otzidente sunt "
"andadas a in antis finas a sa fortificatzione de sa rughe de caminos, e "
"l'ant leada cun pagu resistèntzia. Ant mandadu esploradores a sud e a nord "
"pro cumprèndere comente s'acurtziaiant sas àteras coalitziones, mentras sa "
"parte prus manna de sas tropas andaiat cara a Loneford, chi no aiat "
"defensas. In su sud, sas fortzas de Otzidente aiant passadu su riu e fiant "
"in s'oru de oriente, andende cara a Sullengard. In su tzentru, sas fortzas "
"de èlite de Stoutford ant ischitzadu sa milìtzia mìsera e ant postu a fortza "
"in sas filas issoro sa guàrdia de sa bidda, giustu in tempus, ca Lord Emeric "
"e sas tropas suas fiant arribende dae oriente. At cumintzadu sa Batalla de "
"Fallhaven. Sos corpos ruiant dae cada parte. Sos gherreris de èlite de "
"Stoutford, intostados, resistiant a mala pena contra a sas fortzas numerosas "
"de Nor City. Fallhaven at brusiadu, e sos abitantes suos sunt istados "
"custrintos a si cuare o a fuire. Sos tzitadinos prus ricos fiant giai fuidos "
"a Feygard, giughende·si sos benes issoro. In su sud, sas tropas de sa "
"coalitzione de otzidente si sunt iscontradas cun sas fortzas de sa "
"coalitzione de oriente, ghiadas dae su Barone Benzimos. Sos duos esèrtzitos "
"si sunt iscontrados, e sa Coalitzione de Otzidente est istada custrinta a si "
"difèndere. Cun su riu a palas, ant seberadu de si ritirare, isperende de "
"formare una lìnia de defensa in su ponte e de difèndere su costadu de sud de "
"Stoutford. Sos cabos, chi sos nòmines issoro si sunt pèrdidos in s'istòria, "
"si sunt ritirados de presse, e ant patidu medas pèrdidas. Su progetu pro "
"leare Sullengard fiat faddidu. A nord, sas tropas de Stoutford ant leadu "
"Loneford chene fadiga. Sos esploradores no ant bidu perunu movimentu de sa "
"coalitzione de su nord. Sas fortzas tzentrales de Lord Emeric si sunt luego "
"mòvidas pro si leare sa rughe de caminos, e b'at àpidu cumbatas minores "
"longu s'Àndala Duleiana. In su matessi tempus, s'esèrtzitu de sa Coalitzione "
"de Oriente, ghiadu dae su Duca Vergas, chi non si fidaiat de sos movimentos "
"de Feygard, at mandadu esploradores a nord pro cumprèndere sa risposta de sa "
"Coalitzione de su Nord, mentras sas fortzas suas s'acurtziaiant pro s'aunire "
"cun sas de Brimhaven. Custa situatzione est sighida pro medas annos. Sas "
"batallas si sunt fatas cumbatas minores, ca totu sas duas coalitziones "
"evitaiant cada iscontru detzisivu, ca non cheriant arriscare sa vida de sas "
"tropas issoro. Totu sas duas partes fiant acampadas fora de sas ruinas de "
"Fallhaven, chi sighiant a brusiare. In su sud, su Riu Sutdover s'est fatu sa "
"lìnia chi las partziat, mentras in su nord b'aiat cumbatas minores in su "
"padente intre Brimhaven e Loneford. Sa Coalitzione de su Nord no aiat fatu "
"ancora perunu movimentu. Su puntu mortu longu at creadu una seguresa farsa. "
"Sos presìdios de sos campamentos chi depiant amparare sos costados de su "
"nord de totu sas duas coalitziones si sunt minimados a pagu a pagu, ca sas "
"fortzas printzipales teniant bisòngiu de rinfortzos pro torrare a prènere "
"sas filas. B'at àpidu una paghe pagu segura, chi at dadu a cada parte su "
"tempus de si nde pesare pro una batalla detzisiva. Sa gherra at mustradu sos "
"puntos fortes e sos puntos dèbiles de totu sas duas partes. Sa Coalitzione "
"de Oriente, cun s'apògiu de Nor City, teniat richesas e òmines a muntones, "
"ma fiat tropu ispartzinada, cun sas fortzas suas tropu a tesu s'una de "
"s'àtera. Sa Coalitzione de Otzidente podiat cumbàtere contra a sas fortzas "
"prus mannas de Oriente pro more de sa positzione sua e ca fiat a curtzu a su "
"tzentru de podere de sa coalitzione, in Stoutford. S'ùnicu problema fiat su "
"nùmeru de òmines, ma s'Otzidente impreaiat comente fanteria sos presoneris "
"de sas minieras, e su grupu de èlite de sos gherreris suos resessiat a "
"fàghere de unu disvantàgiu de nùmeru una cumbata a pari. Pensende a custu, "
"Lord Emeric at pensadu unu progetu. Cheriat leare Fallhaven e pònnere in "
"seguru su sìmbulu de su re dae sa tumba de su re Luthor. Diat àere atiradu a "
"tesu sos rinfortzos de Erwin in Fallhaven cun un'atacu dae su sud, e pustis "
"diat àere atacadu sa Coalitzione de Otzidente in Fallhaven. At cumintzadu su "
"perìodu de sa Segunda Gherra. S'Oriente at afortiadu s'esèrtzitu suo de su "
"sud ghiadu dae su Barone Benzimos, e l'at ordinadu de atacare su ponte e de "
"lu leare a cale si siat costu. Custu progetu at funtzionadu, e at causadu su "
"pànicu in su tzentru de sas tropas de Otzidente. Sas ruinas de Fallhaven, "
"como unu terrenu chi fumaiat ancora, tropu a tesu dae sas àndalas suas "
"cobertas de màrmaru e dae sos palatzos ricos suos, fiant disputadas cun "
"cumbatas minores belle cada die. Sos rinfortzos dae Stoutford e dae "
"Abbaniedda ant permìtidu a sa coalitzione de Otzidente de mantènnere sa "
"lìnia sua, ma s'avantzada a s'ispessada dae su sud at obligadu a "
"cuntzentrare in su Sutdover sos sordados noos. Cando sos movimentos sunt "
"andados comente cheriat su progetu de sa Coalitzione de Oriente, Lord Emeric "
"at aunidu sas tropas suas. At cumintzadu sa Segunda Batalla de Fallhaven. "
"Prus manna e prus brutale de sa prima, a pustis de meses e meses de cumbata, "
"totu sas duas partes ant pèrdidu chèntinas de sordados. Sas fortzas de Lord "
"Emeric, chi pariat chi aerent bintu sos inimigos issoro, ant cumintzadu a "
"andare a in antis cara a otzidente. In cussu matessi tempus, est sutzèdidu "
"su chi si podiat isetare. At cumintzadu su de tres perìodu de sas Gherras de "
"sos Nòbiles. Sas tropas de Feygard si sunt mòvidas totu in una cara a sud "
"dae Feygard e dae Thalgard, ant ischitzadu sos presìdios minores postos pro "
"si difèndere dae su nord e sunt andadas a leare Loneford e Brimhaven. In "
"Brimhaven, sos cabos si sunt postos in pànicu e ant cambiadu parte, e una "
"parte de sas tropas de Oriente ghiadas dae su Duca Vergas at sighidu a "
"Brimhaven in sa rebellia sua e at cambiadu parte. Vergas, chi fiat fidele a "
"Nor City, est fuidu a Portu Lughente cun sas tropas chi li fiant abarradas. "
"Loneford est istada leada a lestru, e s'avantzada de sa coalitzione de su "
"nord cara a Fallhaven fiat pro arribare. Sa Coalitzione de Oriente est "
"istada sa prima a si nde ritirare, cun sas fortzas de su Barone Benzimos chi "
"si sunt ritiradas a sa fortalesa de Sullengard. Sas tropas de Lord Emeric "
"chi fiant abarradas si sunt mòvidas a sud-est longu sa Duleiana. Lord Geomyr "
"at partzidu sas fortzas suas in duas: una at sighidu a s'esèrtzitu de Lord "
"Emeric, e s'àtera est andada a leare su chi abarraiat de Fallhaven. In Portu "
"Lughente, sas tropas de Feygard si sunt iscontradas cun sa resistèntzia chi "
"sas tropas abarradas de su Duca Vergas aiant organizadu de presse, e sunt "
"resèssidas a las pònnere in fuga, leende Portu Lughente. Feygard at leadu "
"Fallhaven e Crossglen, e pustis est andada cara a Stoutford, in ue sa "
"coalitzione de otzidente si preparaiat a un'assèdiu. Sas tropas de Feygard "
"ant atzapadu sas tropas de sa coalitzione de Oriente chi fuiant e ant dadu "
"unu corfu devastadore a sas fortzas istracas. Su Barone Benzimos at lassadu "
"unu contingente piticu a difèndere Sullengard e est andadu a agiudare su "
"sennore suo in sa Batalla de su padente chi como est malaitu. Sos "
"bidditzolos de Abbaniedda sunt istados comporados pro chi lassarent de dare "
"apògiu a sa Coalitzione de Otzidente; a sos cabos issoro ant lassadu sa "
"vida. Sos de Feygard ant postu s'assèdiu a Stoutford, ant leadu a Lord Erwin "
"e l'ant giustitziadu, cun sos membros de sa casada Garland chi fiant ancora "
"bios. Sa batalla detzisiva intre sas tropas de Feygard e sa coalitzione de "
"Oriente est acabbada cun su Barone Benzimos chi s'est betadu chene giudìtziu "
"contra a sas filas de sos cavalieris de Feygard armados de totu puntu. E "
"custu l'at giutu a sa morte. Lord Emeric est istadu mortu dae una fritza "
"pèrdida, e petzi una de tres partes de sas tropas est torrada a Nor City. Sa "
"casada Welfort at leadu su controllu e at firmadu unu tratadu cun Feygard. "
"Lord Geomyr est istadu coronadu re, e custu at sinnadu sa fine de sa gherra."

