#: itemlist_undertell.json:undertell_book
msgid "Undertell: Its Ghosts and History"
msgstr "Undertell: sos pantasmas e s'istòria sua"

#: itemlist_undertell.json:undertell_book:description
msgid ""
"Undertell: Its Ghosts and History\n"
"\n"
"Few places in Dhayavar inspire as much dread and fascination as the caverns beneath Mt. Galmore. Known collectively as Undertell, these depths have claimed the lives of miners, soldiers, scholars, and fortune-seekers alike.\n"
"\n"
"What follows is a collected account of the known and suspected truths of Undertell, compiled from fragmented records, hearsay, and personal investigation.\n"
"\n"
"Chapter I: The Mines Beneath the Mountain\n"
"\n"
"It is beyond dispute that Undertell was once heavily mined. Gold veins, rare gems, and other valuable stones were extracted here for decades. Even now, abandoned tunnels and collapsed shafts bear unmistakable marks of pick and flame.\n"
"\n"
"Though the mines were eventually sealed, it is widely believed that much wealth remains undisturbed in the deeper reaches. Fear, not scarcity, ended the mining operations.\n"
"\n"
"Those brave or foolish enough to venture below still return with traces of gold, confirming that the mountain has not yet given up all it holds.\n"
"\n"
"Chapter II: Miner's Sickness\n"
"\n"
"Those who labored in the caverns beneath Undertell spoke of a sickness that came not from the air or the water, but from the stones themselves. At first, it was subtle. Miners complained of a bitter taste that lingered on the tongue after long hours in the tunnels. Their breath grew sour, and their sleep was broken by strange dreams of distant fires, of voices echoing through stone, of light burning behind closed eyes.\n"
"\n"
"The sickness did not strike all who entered Undertell, only those who worked near the deeper seams, where the heartstone grew thickest in the rock. Those who merely passed through the caverns did not feel its touch. Those who lingered, who carved it free with bare hands and iron tools, carried something back with them when they returned to the surface. Not a curse.\n"
"\n"
"Chapter III: On Ghosts and Lingering Spirits\n"
"\n"
"Many claim Undertell is haunted. Travelers speak of pale figures watching from afar, whispers echoing through stone and shapes that vanish when approached.\n"
"\n"
"Some insist these are the dead miners, bound by unfinished labor. Others claim the spirits are something older, drawn to the mountain long before any pick struck rock.\n"
"\n"
"There is no agreement on whether these ghosts are hostile. Accounts vary wildly, some explorers report being ignored entirely, while others describe sudden violence without warning.\n"
"\n"
"Chapter IV: The Lethgar and the Elytharans\n"
"\n"
"Two distinct groups of spirits are frequently mentioned in surviving accounts.\n"
"\n"
"The Lethgar are described as orderly, almost disciplined, haunting areas closest to the old mining routes. Some believe they were guards or overseers in life.\n"
"\n"
"The Elytharans, by contrast, appear scattered and erratic. Their presence is strongest near collapsed tunnels and forgotten chambers. Whether they are miners, prisoners, or something else entirely remains unclear.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible these distinctions are imagined by fearful minds seeking patterns where none exist.\n"
"\n"
"Chapter V: Of Darkness and the Shadow\n"
"\n"
"Many who venture into Undertell report an oppressive presence - a weight that presses upon the mind and spirit alike. Some describe it as the Shadow itself, seeping from the stone.\n"
"\n"
"Others argue this sensation is merely the result of isolation, darkness, and lingering fear passed down through generations.\n"
"\n"
"There is no proof that Undertell is the source of the Shadow, only that the two are often spoken of together.\n"
"\n"
"Chapter VI: Creatures of the Deep\n"
"\n"
"Beyond spirits, there are reports of creatures inhabiting the lower caverns. Some resemble twisted men, others living shadows given form.\n"
"\n"
"Whether these beings are monsters, spirits, or something else entirely is a matter of debate. Few witnesses survive long enough to offer clear descriptions.\n"
"\n"
"Still, enough similar accounts exist to suggest that Undertell is not empty and that something watches those who descend too far.\n"
"\n"
"Chapter VII: A Warning to the Curious\n"
"\n"
"Undertell rewards greed as often as it punishes it. For every tale of riches recovered, there are three of those who never returned.\n"
"\n"
"If knowledge is sought, tread carefully. If wealth is desired, expect to pay for it.\n"
"\n"
"[the remaining pages are soaked in blood and thus unreadable.]"
msgstr ""
"Undertell: sos pantasmas e s'istòria sua\n"
"\n"
"Pagos logos in Dhayavar ispirant tanta timòria e tanta curiosidade cantu sas "
"grutas suta de su Monte Galmore. Connotas totu impare comente Undertell, "
"custas profundidades ant leadu sa vida a minadores, sordados, istudiosos e "
"chircadores de fortuna.\n"
"\n"
"Su chi sighit est unu contu de sas veridades connotas e suspetadas de "
"Undertell, regortu dae registros a bìculos, dae sas boghes de sa gente e dae "
"indàgines personales.\n"
"\n"
"Capìtulu I: Sas minieras suta de su monte\n"
"\n"
"Non b'at dùbbiu chi una borta in Undertell bi fiant minieras mannas. Pro "
"dècadas nd'ant bogadu venas de oro, gemmas raras e àteras pedras de valore. "
"Fintzas como, sos tunnels abbandonados e sos putzos de mina rutos tenent "
"sinnos de picu e de fogu chi non si podent confùndere.\n"
"\n"
"Mancari sas minieras sunt istadas serradas, medas creent chi in sas partes "
"prus fundudas b'apat ancora richesas mannas chi nemos at tocadu. Est istada "
"sa timòria, e non sa mancàntzia de richesa, a pònnere fine a su traballu de "
"sas minieras.\n"
"\n"
"Sos chi sunt bastante coragiosos, o bastante macos, pro falare a giosso "
"torrant ancora cun rastros de oro, e custu cunfirmat chi su monte no at "
"ancora dadu totu su chi tenet.\n"
"\n"
"Capìtulu II: Su male de sos minadores\n"
"\n"
"Sos chi traballaiant in sas grutas suta de Undertell contaiant de unu male "
"chi non beniat dae s'àera o dae s'abba, ma dae sas pedras etotu. A su "
"cumintzu fiat lèbiu. Sos minadores si lamentaiant de unu sabore amargu chi "
"lis abarraiat in sa limba a pustis de oras longas in sos tunnels. S'àlidu "
"issoro si faghiat agru, e su sonnu issoro beniat truncadu dae bisos istranos "
"de fogos a tesu, de boghes chi resonaiant in mesu de sa pedra, de lughe chi "
"brusiaiat a palas de sos ogros serrados.\n"
"\n"
"Su male non tocaiat a totu sos chi intraiant in Undertell, petzi a sos chi "
"traballaiant a curtzu de sas venas prus fundudas, in ue sa pedra de coro "
"creschiat prus ispissa in sa roca. Sos chi passaiant petzi in mesu de sas "
"grutas non nde intendiant su tocu. Sos chi b'abarraiant, chi la bogaiant cun "
"sas manos nudas e cun ainas de ferru, giughiant cun issos calicuna cosa "
"cando torraiant a sa superfìtzie. No una maleditzione.\n"
"\n"
"Capìtulu III: Subra de sos pantasmas e de sos ispìritos chi abarrant\n"
"\n"
"Medas narant chi Undertell est infestadu de pantasmas. Sos biagiadores "
"contant de figuras pàllidas chi abbàidant dae a tesu, de murmutos chi "
"resonant in mesu de sa pedra e de formas chi isparint cando t'acùrtzias.\n"
"\n"
"Unos cantos insistent chi siant sos minadores mortos, ligados a unu traballu "
"chi no ant acabbadu. Àteros narant chi sos ispìritos siant una cosa prus "
"antiga, atirada a su monte meda in antis chi perunu picu aeret corfidu sa "
"roca.\n"
"\n"
"Non b'at acordu subra de si custos pantasmas siant ostiles. Sos contos sunt "
"diferentes meda: unos cantos esploradores narant chi los ant ignorados de su "
"totu, mentras àteros contant de violèntzias a s'ispessada, chene perunu "
"avisu.\n"
"\n"
"Capìtulu IV: Sos Lethgar e sos elytharanos\n"
"\n"
"In sos contos chi nos sunt arribados si mentovant a s'ispissu duos grupos "
"distintos de ispìritos.\n"
"\n"
"Sos Lethgar sunt descritos comente ordinados, belle disciplinados, e "
"infestant sas àreas prus a curtzu de sos caminos de mina antigos. Unos "
"cantos creent chi in vida esserent guàrdias o cabos de traballu.\n"
"\n"
"Sos elytharanos, a s'imbesse, parent ispartos e chene òrdine. Sa presèntzia "
"issoro est prus forte a curtzu de sos tunnels rutos e de sas càmeras "
"ismentigadas. Si siant minadores, presoneris o una cosa de su totu "
"diferente, no est ancora craru.\n"
"\n"
"Podet èssere chi custas distintziones las apant immaginadas mentes "
"timoriosas chi chircant modellos in ue non bi nd'at.\n"
"\n"
"Capìtulu V: S'iscuriu e s'Umbra\n"
"\n"
"Medas de sos chi s'arriscant in Undertell contant de una presèntzia chi "
"oprimet - unu pesu chi carcat subra de sa mente e de s'ispìritu a pari. Unos "
"cantos la descrient comente s'Umbra etotu, chi essit dae sa pedra.\n"
"\n"
"Àteros sustenent chi custa sensatzione siat petzi su risultadu de "
"s'isulamentu, de s'iscuriu e de una timòria chi si trasmitit dae "
"generatziones.\n"
"\n"
"Non b'at peruna proa chi Undertell siat sa fonte de s'Umbra, petzi chi de "
"totu sos duos si faeddat a s'ispissu paris.\n"
"\n"
"Capìtulu VI: Sas creaduras de su profundu\n"
"\n"
"A parte sos ispìritos, b'at contos de creaduras chi bivent in sas grutas "
"prus fundudas. Unas cantas assimìgiant a òmines tortos, àteras a umbras bias "
"chi ant leadu forma.\n"
"\n"
"Si custos èsseres siant mostros, ispìritos o una cosa de su totu diferente "
"est unu tema de discussione. Pagos testimòngios bivent bastante pro dare "
"descritziones craras.\n"
"\n"
"Su matessi, b'at bastantes contos simigiantes pro fàghere pensare chi "
"Undertell no est bòidu e chi calicuna cosa abbàidat a sos chi falant tropu a "
"fundu.\n"
"\n"
"Capìtulu VII: Un'avisu pro sos curiosos\n"
"\n"
"Undertell prèmiat sa gana de richesa a s'ispissu cantu la punit. Pro cada "
"contu de richesas agatadas, b'at tres contos de sos chi non sunt mai "
"torrados.\n"
"\n"
"Si chircas connoschèntzia, camina cun cura. Si disìgias richesa, iseta·ti de "
"la pagare.\n"
"\n"
"[sas pàginas chi abarrant sunt infustas de sàmbene e duncas non si podent "
"lèghere.]"

